A5 Part 3.4: Three alternative uses of our public API

Public API used by all three:
https://ilona.pythonanywhere.com/api/quest-summary/
No login needed. Returns JSON: [{"quest": ..., "category": ..., "user_count": ...}, ...]
(anonymous totals per quest, so no personal data is exposed)


01_quest_summary_api.py: Python script (quest report)
A developer or community volunteer can call our public API from any Python
script with the requests library, without an account or login. The script
requests the production API, receives a JSON list with each quest's name,
category, and number of users who completed it, and prints it as a table.
It then aggregates the data: total completions and percentage share per
category, the most and least popular quests (listing ties), and the average
per quest. A SafeSpace admin could use this to see which quests need
more promotion.

02_quest_statistics_notebook.py: Statistical analysis in a notebook (pandas)
A data analyst can load the same public API straight into a pandas DataFrame
in a Jupyter notebook. The notebook computes
summary statistics of completions per quest (mean, median, standard
deviation, min, max), each quest's percentage share and difference from the
average, and totals and averages per category with groupby. It then plots a
bar chart of users per quest, colored by category, with the average marked
and saved as quest_statistics.png. This shows the API can feed research or
reporting without touching our database directly.

03_export_to_excel.py: Importing into Excel
People who don't program, such as a student club, can use the
API through a spreadsheet. The script downloads the JSON from the production
API and builds safespace_quests.xlsx: a "Quests" sheet with the raw data
(Quest, Category, User Count) plus Excel SUM and AVERAGE formulas, and a
"By Category" sheet that totals users per category with SUMIF formulas and
shows a bar chart. In Excel they can then sort, filter, build pivot tables,
and share the file, reusing the same endpoint that powers our Vega-Lite chart.
